Ne2 Bb7 {! Aitken} 9. f3 g6 10. c4 {! Aitken} Bg7 11. Nbc3 Ne7 12. Be3 O-O 13.
O-O Rb8 14. Qd2 Bc8 15. Rad1 ({Roger Paige gives} 15. Rfd1 {in his book of Sir
George Thomas's games.}) 15... Be6 16. b3 f5 {? Aitken} 17. Bh6 fxe4 {(Aitken
clearly has 18.Nf4 Qc1 19.Bxg7 Kxg7 here. 18.Nf4?? loses to 18...Bxh6 and is
too simple to miss by two good players, I have given 18.Bxg7 and then Nf4 - GC.
Roger Paige's book has 18 Bxg7 as GC has given here.)} 18. Bxg7 Kxg7 19. Nf4
Qc8 20. Nxe4 Nc6 21. Ng5 ({Roger Paige's book, which had an earlier 15 Rfd1,
now has} 21. Rfe1 Nd4 22. Ng5 {after which the two versions converge - JS})
21... Nd4 22. Rfe1 Re8 23. Qc3 Bf7 24. Rxe8 Qxe8 25. Re1 Qd7 26. Nfe6+ Bxe6 27.
Nxe6+ Kg8 28. Nxd4 cxd4 29. Qxd4 Re8 30. Rxe8+ Qxe8 31. Qe4 Qf8 32. h3 Qf6 33.
Kh2 Qb2 {? Aitken} 34. Qe7 {! Aitken} Qd2 35. Qd8+ Kg7 36. Qxc7+ Kh6 {? Aitken}
