g5 43. Qf7+ Kh4 44. Qg6 {Source: Aitken Scorebook 7 & Times Weekly Edition, 9
January 1946, p19 (as given in The Chess Games of Sir George Alan Thomas by by
Roger L Paige (2005)). (Final table of this tournament is shown in BCM,
December 1945, p284: 1 G Wood 8/10, 2 Dr PM List 7½, 3 Dr O Friedman 7, 4 Sir
G Thomas 6½, 5-6 Dr JM Aitken, WL Brierley 5½, 7-8 H Brown, AF Truscott 5, 9
A Distler 2½, 10 GH Diggle 2, 11 RE Hayley ½.)} 1-0

